              "exploit_scenario": "From their own machine the attacker starts a passkey login at https://victim.example and gets the server challenge. Script they injected into the victim's https://victim.example page calls navigator.credentials.get({publicKey:{challenge, rpId:'victim.example', allowCredentials:[{type:'public-key', id:<victim credential id>}]}}). The MAIN-world wrapper relays the request, the background admits it without user activation, selectPasskey finds the one listed credential, and the Worker signs authenticatorData with UP|UV|BE|BS set. The ADR 0021 D re-prompt does not apply because allowCredentials is not empty. No window or prompt appears. The relay posts the assertion to the page, the script sends it to the attacker, and the attacker completes the login on their device as the victim. A native WebAuthn request would need the user to interact with the browser's prompt.",
